WEBVTT

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.230
What happened? What's going on?

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.070
Hurry up and do something!

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.780
Can't we warp?

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.190
Escape shuttles don't have that kind of equipment.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.290
The real wind,
the real sea

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.090
Everyone, are you okay?

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.210
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.820
Where's the gravity storm?

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:35.830
How does it look?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.830
I can't see anything.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.140
The instruments seem to all be broken.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.030
Maybe we weathered the storm.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.980
Even if that were true...

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:50.700
I guess that gravity storm
wasn't such a big deal after all.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.740
What's going on up there?

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:57.560
Only our shuttle seems to have been left behind.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.310
That can't be!

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.580
But why just this shuttle?

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.480
Shingo! After you came in here,
you were touching all sorts of switches!

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.560
It's definitely because of that!

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.870
If that's it, then how about you, Howard?

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.240
What's that?

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.540
Wait! We'll look into that later.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.900
Exactly! We still don't
know if we're going to be rescued.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.010
Shingo, can you figure out where the shuttle is?

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.380
I don't think we should be
that far from our colony yet, but...

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.230
First off, we should turn on the rescue beacon.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.490
I am the computer installed in this craft, M-17.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.020
M-17, where are we?

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.800
That is impossible to determine.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.760
Can we send out the emergency beacon?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:54.510
That is impossible.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.170
This thing is useless.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.130
Why is that?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:05.030
This craft will momentarily
enter a planet's gravity well.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.310
Please fasten your seatbelts.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.040
Gravity well?

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.720
Did we get close to some planet?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:26.190
Earth?

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.640
That's impossible.

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:32.190
Yeah, Earth already stopped being a blue planet.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.480
Then what planet is that?

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.810
The former earth?

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.930
Are you saying we flew through time?

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.380
It might not be impossible in space.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.230
Have we come to the world of long ago?

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.650
If so, what's going to happen to us?

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.210
Stop being ridiculous!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:53.270
I can't take it anymore!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.010
Will you give it a rest?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.090
Hurry up and do something!

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.590
What is this thing?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.430
Whaddaya mean, "This thing?"

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.110
I have a proper name, you know! It's Chako!

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.160
--I'm sorry! She's my robot pet!
--Idiot, let go of me!

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.890
You thought it was okay
to bring something like that along?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.380
"Something?" I'm not a thing!

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.140
I knew that, but there was a little mistake, and...

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.610
You knew?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.570
The shuttle getting left behind is that thing's fault!

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.980
That's just silly!

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:26.890
It's obviously true!

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.630
You two are going to take responsibility for this!

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.560
Howard, calm down!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:37.240
Exactly! The shuttle wouldn't cut itself
loose just because an extra animal got on!

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.070
Then how come this happened?

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.530
As usual, you're a barking dog.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.120
What?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.540
More importantly, is it okay
to be getting so close to the planet?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.450
This craft is beginning its
approach to land on the planet.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.280
We will enter the atmosphere momentarily.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.040
All passengers, please take
your seats and fasten your seatbelts.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.210
Landing?

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.890
Even though we don't know what planet that is?

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.910
M-17, can we avoid it?

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.030
It is impossible.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:16.200
This craft will momentarily enter the atmosphere.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:19.590
M-17, are we equipped for that?

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.690
Now landing under autopilot control.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.140
Okay, everyone, let's take our seats.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.380
State of emergency entered.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.670
Due to the damage to the ship,
activation of autopilot is impossible.

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.300
What did you say?

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.940
The gravity storm must have affected the computer.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:46.460
Computer system cannot return to normal operation.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.110
Reserve systems cannot be activated.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.080
Performing forced shut-down.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.910
Wait! What do we do
when we enter the atmosphere?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.230
Computer system... down...

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:02.630
What's going to happen?

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.250
At this rate, we'll be destroyed by the atmosphere.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.390
The shuttle's going to burn out?

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:08.490
What?

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.800
We're going to die?

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:12.800
Stop kidding me!

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.490
You think I can die in a place like this?

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.490
Calm down! Isn't there anything we can do?

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:24.150
We should be able to fly it manually,
but without knowing the angle of approach...

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.590
But, the computer...

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:28.840
Chako!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.690
You finally remembered I'm here.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.030
Gauges're all busted, huh?

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.220
Ah well, it'll work out somehow.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.710
Guidance calculations okay.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.640
Entry angle calculated.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.760
Autopilot is impossible after all.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.760
Luna, take the helm.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.090
Wait How do we know you...

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.570
Luna, do you have experience?

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.480
It's my first atmospheric entry...

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:28.050
...but I have piloted an escape capsule before.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:29.780
Can you do it?

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.310
We have no choice but to let her try.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:33.710
I think so too.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:34.860
Me too.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:36.090
Me too.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.040
Bell, damn you!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.390
Okay, we'll leave it to Luna.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.580
Everyone else, take your seats.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:57.790
First off, you hafta point the ship straight.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:01.520
Press the left button on the lever,
and the jet propulsion switches will come out.

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.460
First is roll.

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:06.840
Push the bottom left switch for two seconds.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:10.670
Stop.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.190
Next is top left for two seconds.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:18.190
Stop.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.080
Next we have to lift the nose.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.820
Top for three and a half seconds.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.890
Sixteen above level. We're entering nose first.

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.810
Close the heat-resistant shutters.
It's the bottom right lever.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.120
Roger.

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.370
There should be some
switches lined up at your upper left.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.610
Those operate the cooling system.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.380
These?

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.060
Cooling system activated.

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.030
Entering atmosphere.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.010
Outer wall temperature rising.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.380
Set cooling to maximum.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.390
There's a lever on that last panel, right?

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:13.560
This one?

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.180
Cooling system at maximum.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:18.600
What's next?

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:19.730
That's all.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.330
From here on we leave it in the hands of fate.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.230
Airspeed good.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:49.860
Altitude 25,000.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.180
Luna, we made it through.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:53.270
Really?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.500
Open the front shutter.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:56.550
Roger!

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.160
Are those... clouds?

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:02.030
Yep.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.390
Real clouds.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:05.480
I guess we succeeded.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.370
It's a little early to celebrate.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.210
Set the nose back.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.350
Roger.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.680
What is this?

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.090
It's lightning.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.280
It's my first time seein' the real thing too.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.640
After the lightin' comes the rain.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:41.480
What should I do?

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:43.480
Can you see the ground?

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.560
It seems like just ocean.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.190
Alright, we'll land on the water.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.590
Raise the nose.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.470
Roger! I'll give it a try.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.650
Luna... are you awake yet?

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:14.720
Chako...

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.890
Ah! How's everyone?

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.310
Safe. Nobody seems to be hurt.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.520
Everyone, wake up!

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:32.610
Sharla.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:34.890
Howard.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:35.910
Howard!

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.060
Luna...

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.830
What happened to us?

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:45.170
It looks like we survived somehow.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.000
The sea!

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.210
The clouds are moving.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:01.760
It's the sun.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.510
I wonder where this is.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.380
That sun's the real thing, right?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.950
It's obviously a man-made sun.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.590
But this doesn't seem like the inside of a colony.

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:19.800
That's right! Those clouds and the sea
right in front of us don't seem to be man-made.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:21.390
That's really the sun!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:23.940
It's the first time I've felt this.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:28.160
It's warm and soft and gives me a happy feeling.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:29.740
It's true.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:34.070
If you're saying that's the real sun,
then this is Earth after all?

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:38.760
I ain't sure about that, but the atmosphere's
composition seems to be like Earth's.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:39.430
Wha'?

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:43.650
Come to think of it, we've
been breathing this last while, but...

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:47.340
The shuttle's systems are
supplying us with Oxygen, right?

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.670
All those're totally busted.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.580
Wha'!?

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.540
What'cha gettin' all surprised about now?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.990
We've been breathin' this
planet's atmosphere for a while.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.180
Lookee here!

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:05.140
The outside air's gettin' in through here.

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.230
Is the air's composition okay?

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:17.380
It doesn't have anythin' toxic, but the amount of Carbon Dioxide is five times normal.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:20.210
Don't worry.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.280
That's well within your tolerance.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:24.230
The seawater is okay, too.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:26.980
Yeesh! What's going on here, anyway?

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:30.130
Can we send out the rescue beacon?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.730
Can't. The shuttle's systems're all totally busted.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.220
Then there's nothing we can do?

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:43.410
They should have noticed on the ship
that our escape shuttle was cut loose.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:48.190
That's right. They'll have realised we're
gone by now and will start looking for us.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:51.580
Then we're supposed to hang out
here like this until help comes?

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:56.160
Anyways, let's open the hatch
and see how things look outside.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:57.980
Agreed!

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.260
The wind feels nice!

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.870
It seems like a real world.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:21.020
A real sun, the real sea, real clouds, and the real wind.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.810
--I'm gonna look too
--Let me see! Let me see!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.960
I wanna see too!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.300
Beautiful!

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:28.990
They certainly look real.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.530
Don't they?

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.530
--Somebody move and let me see too.
--Is the real sea like a giant puddle?

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:35.140
There!

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:43.280
It's land.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:47.210
It's true!

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:48.620
Land, land!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:51.390
There's foliage.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.260
Maybe there are animals too!

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.530
Can we swim there?

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.930
It's dangerous, and furthermore, far.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:02.440
I've certainly never swum in a real sea.

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.090
Oh yeah! Maybe there's some equipment in the shuttle!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:09.110
Then let's look around for it!

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:23.330
Here!

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.280
There's a boat!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:28.800
There's a laser gun, too!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.130
And a knife and a mini-light!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.130
There's a sewing set...

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:34.930
...there's more...

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:37.950
...Mineral water and emergency rations.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:43.430
What, this is all?

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.430
Let's distribute them among us.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.970
One of each for each person.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:53.530
We don't know when we'll be able to refill them.
Everyone manage their own eating and drinking.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.700
We'll save the rest for later.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.230
Don't talk so miserly.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.840
There's sure to be something when we reach shore.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.930
We don't know that for certain.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:07.370
Shut up!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:08.870
I certainly know it!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.720
What will you do if we find a dangerous animal?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.030
When it happens, I'll use this.

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:16.800
You can use it?

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:20.190
Papa took me hunting lots of times.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:25.140
By hunting, you mean shooting
at special animal robots, right?

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.450
If you ask me, that's a dangerous hobby.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.550
It's something nobles have a taste for.

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:31.540
After all, it's just a game.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:32.760
What?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:33.990
Stop it!

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.240
At least while you're holding something so dangerous!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.380
I'll show you my skills sometime soon.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:51.300
Are you really going alone?

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:53.890
Yeah, just me will be plenty.

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:55.880
I'll go with you.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.080
I don't need you.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:58.930
It'll be faster with two.

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:01.110
And you plan to row by yourself?

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:05.960
Do what you want.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:27.860
Alright.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:36.080
Hold it still!

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.840
Will he really be okay?

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.210
Menori, here.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.220
Luna, I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:54.390
Be careful.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:56.850
Howard.

00:20:01.520 --> 00:20:02.780
Okay, let go.

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:16.090
Luna.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:18.450
We're depending on you.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:24.620
While Menori ain't here,
everyone's countin' on you to protect us.

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:25.990
Keep your head clear.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:35.510
We're turning.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.780
Row more reliably!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:40.730
I know! That's what I'm doing!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.470
What just happened?

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:47.760
I couldn't see the waves coming from behind.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.580
That's why I said it was dangerous!

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.090
This is why swimming across is unrealistic!

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.910
Keep it up!

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.170
Keep going!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:04.820
Fight!

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:18.920
Luna, Kaoru is...

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:28.220
What's wrong?

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.510
Let's call them back.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:31.690
Look!

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.880
What's that?

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:39.210
What is it, what is it?

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:40.800
What can you see?

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:42.260
Big trouble!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:43.890
There's a weird animal!

00:21:44.310 --> 00:21:45.380
What did you say?

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.880
It's going after the boat!

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:51.560
Hey!

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.120
--Menori!
--Menori!

00:21:54.410 --> 00:21:55.730
Menori!

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:57.280
Come back!

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.410
Hey!

00:21:58.730 --> 00:22:00.040
It's dangerous!

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.370
Come back!

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:03.660
I'm all worn out.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:06.620
Keep going! If you give up, we're done for!

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:18.110
It's stopped.

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.060
It's true! We've stopped!

00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:23.510
It seems like we got away from them somehow.

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:24.860
Come back!

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:26.060
Hey!

00:22:26.230 --> 00:22:27.840
Hurry back!

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:28.930
Come back!

00:22:28.930 --> 00:22:30.600
It's dangerous!

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:31.200
Come back!

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:32.360
Hey!

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.900
Howard!

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:36.320
Below you! Below!

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:37.990
Did he say below?

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:03.510
What's up, what's up?

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:05.680
That's a flashy welcome!

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:08.140
Otherwise I might not've noticed.

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:12.690
Wrong, wrong, Chako! It's aiming for us!

00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:13.580
What?

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:17.720
That's right! It's because I'm a little more attractive!

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:21.830
Too bad, after you guys ignored me for so long.

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:24.750
Just stay away forever!

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:29.490
Next time: What's going to happen to us!?
